{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Fast whoosh",
  "description": "A thin bamboo cane swung hard past the ear, 180 ms from start to stop: the air tearing along its length (a hiss that sweeps up to 5 kHz at the fastest point, 80 ms in, and back down) and the whistle of the tip itself, a narrow tone that rises and falls with the speed as the air sheds off the rod. Dry, close, no room.",
  "tags": [
    "movement",
    "whoosh",
    "swish",
    "swing",
    "sword",
    "stick",
    "punch",
    "fast",
    "air"
  ],
